_*.py
_*.log
diagnose*.py
artifacts/dataset_gpu_*.npz
artifacts/ablation_probe.json

# Personal documents. This repository is PUBLIC. A resume with a phone number
# and address lived untracked in the working tree for four days, one `git add
# -A` away from being pushed -- and `git add -A` did get run here once, sweeping
# in unrelated files that had to be unpicked with a soft reset. Keep personal
# documents out of the directory entirely; this is only the backstop.
*resume*
*cv.pdf
*.tex

# Recorded market data. Three subtrees are tracked on purpose and are the
# ground truth behind measured results (see "Data archive size" in README):
#   data/surfaces/      626 gzipped SPY/BTC/ETH captures, 2026-08-20..23
#   data/btc_series/    the Saturday BTC jump-premium series and its logs
#   data/pricing_map*/  the GPU-labelled .npz shards the pricing map trained on
# Everything else under data/ is ignored, and so are NEW recorder captures
# under data/surfaces/ (scripts/record_surfaces.py writes there every few
# minutes when running; that stream grows without bound and is banked
# deliberately with `git add -f`, not swept in by `git add -A`). Files already
# tracked are unaffected by these rules.
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/surfaces/
!data/btc_series/
!data/pricing_map*/
data/surfaces/**/*.json.gz
